    <!-- vmx-invvpid-single-context-noglobals: removed.  Not a real CPU
         feature; qemu 9.2.4 does not expose a property by this name
         (only vmx-invept-single-context-noglobals exists — INVEPT, not
         INVVPID).  Some older QEMU forks may have accepted the unknown
         name silently; mainline 9.2.4 errors with:
           can't apply global Skylake-Server-noTSX-IBRS-x86_64-cpu.
           vmx-invvpid-single-context-noglobals=on: Property ... not found
         which makes qemu exit before the guest starts.  Every win11
         clone bake then ran the 15-minute warmup against shutoff
         domains and snapshotted them in shutoff state, which CAPE
         later rejects with "Snapshot is not in a 'running' state". -->
